.\" Man page for pogoda (imgw-rs). Render: man ./man/pogoda.1
.TH POGODA 1 "2026-08-10" "pogoda 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pogoda \- terminal point\-weather nowcast from IMGW\-PIB
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pogoda
.RI [ "City,CC" " | " "lat,lon" ]
.br
.B pogoda
.BR \-h | \-\-help
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pogoda
prints the current weather for one exact geographic point, taken from the
.B HYBRID
nowcast of
.BR IMGW\-PIB ,
the Polish Institute of Meteorology and Water Management, together with any
meteorological and hydrological (drought) warnings that are active for that
point.
.PP
Because IMGW is a Poland\-only service, the output is written in
.BR Polish .
This manual describes the tool in English, but every label it prints is quoted
below exactly as it appears.
.PP
The location may be given as an argument or read from the configuration file
(see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
It is resolved as follows:
.IP \(bu 3
A
.I City,CC
name (for example
.IR "Warszawa,PL" )
is geocoded to coordinates. The country code is honoured and the Polish name
index is queried, so Polish place names resolve correctly.
.IP \(bu 3
Bare
.I lat,lon
coordinates (for example
.IR "50.06,19.94" )
are used directly; a display name is obtained by reverse geocoding.
.PP
IMGW's HYBRID endpoint serves a forecast for the exact latitude/longitude
rather than for a fixed station, so even a small village reports its own point.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary \(em including the currently configured default
location and the path of the configuration file \(em and exit.
.PP
There are no other options. In particular there is
.B no
.B \-p / \-\-place
flag: the location is always a plain positional argument. An unrecognised
option (any argument beginning with
.RB ` \- ')
is an error.
.SH OUTPUT
Output has three parts, printed top to bottom: active warning boxes (if any),
the current\-conditions block, and a data\-source line.
.SS Current conditions
The main block is headed by a banner:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
 Pogoda: <place> \(em <temp> \(de C, <sky>  (IMGW HYBRID, odczuwalna <feels> \(de C)
.fi
.RE
.PP
followed by these lines (each prefixed with three spaces):
.TP
.B Opady / Deszcz / Śnieg
Precipitation summary for the forecast window (see
.BR "PRECIPITATION" ).
.TP
.B Wiatr
Wind: direction phrase, speed in m/s, bearing in degrees, and gusts
.RI ( "w porywach" ).
.TP
.B Ciśnienie
Mean sea\-level pressure in hPa.
.TP
.B Wilgotność
Relative humidity in percent.
.TP
.B Zachmurzenie
Cloud cover in percent.
.TP
.B Wschód / Zachód
Sunrise and sunset times and the length of the day.
.SS Sky / cloud cover
The banner's sky word uses the IMGW cloud scale:
.TP
.B bezchmurnie
clear sky (at night)
.TP
.B słonecznie
clear sky (during the day)
.TP
.B "zachmurzenie małe"
few clouds
.TP
.B "zachmurzenie umiarkowane"
scattered clouds
.TP
.B "zachmurzenie duże"
broken clouds
.TP
.B "zachmurzenie całkowite"
overcast
.SS Wind
The direction is named after the point of the compass the wind blows
.IR from ,
in the genitive case, following the word
.IR Wiatr :
.RS 4
.nf
N   Wiatr z północy
NE  Wiatr z północnego wschodu
E   Wiatr ze wschodu
SE  Wiatr z południowego wschodu
S   Wiatr z południa
SW  Wiatr z południowego zachodu
W   Wiatr z zachodu
NW  Wiatr z północnego zachodu
.fi
.RE
.SH PRECIPITATION
The precipitation line is deliberately short \(em at most two clauses \(em so a
reader gets the one thing that matters, not a step\-by\-step timeline.
Which form is used depends on whether it is precipitating at the start of the
window:
.TP
.B Raining now
The amount that will fall until it stops, then \(em if it stops before the
window ends \(em how long it stays dry afterwards, e.g.:
.RS
.RS 4
.nf
Deszcz: umiarkowany. 2.1 mm w ciągu najbliższych 6h, potem sucho przez kolejne 21h
.fi
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B Dry now
How long it stays dry, then the amount that falls over the rest of the window:
.RS
.RS 4
.nf
Deszcz: sucho przez najbliższe 16h, potem 2.1 mm w ciągu kolejnych 21h
.fi
.RE
.RE
.TP
.B No precipitation
.RS
.RS 4
.nf
Opady: sucho przez najbliższe 37h
.fi
.RE
.RE
.PP
The leading label reflects the type: pure rain is
.IR Deszcz ,
snow is
.IR Śnieg ,
a mix is
.IR "Deszcz i śnieg" ,
and any other/unknown mix is
.IR Opady .
.SS Rain\-intensity classification
When it is raining
.I now
and the precipitation is pure rain, the label is replaced by an intensity
phrase derived from the current rate in millimetres per hour (mm/h). The rate
comes from the 10\-minute data when available (value \(mu 6), otherwise from the
hourly value. The bands are:
.TP
.B < 0.25 mm/h
.I "Mżawka."
\(em drizzle
.TP
.B 0.25 \(en 2 mm/h
.I "Deszcz: lekki."
\(em light rain
.TP
.B 2 \(en 5 mm/h
.I "Deszcz: umiarkowany."
\(em moderate rain
.TP
.B 5 \(en 10 mm/h
.I "Deszcz: silny."
\(em heavy rain
.TP
.B 10 \(en 15 mm/h
.I "Deszcz: bardzo silny!"
\(em very heavy rain
.TP
.B 15 \(en 30 mm/h
.I "Ulewa!!!"
\(em downpour
.TP
.B > 30 mm/h
.I "Nawałnica!!!"
\(em torrential rain / cloudburst
.PP
Each upper bound is inclusive (a rate of exactly 2 mm/h is still
.IR lekki ).
Snow and mixed precipitation keep their plain type label and are not classified
by intensity.
.SH WARNINGS
Warnings are filtered to the
.I point,
not to the whole country, and are printed as boxes above the forecast.
.TP
.B Meteorological warnings
Captioned
.IR "OSTRZEŻENIE!" ,
with the severity level
.RI ( "stopień" " 1\(en3)"
and, when published, the probability in percent. The box gives the event name,
its validity period
.RI ( "od " ... " do " ...),
and IMGW's description. These come from the nationwide feed, filtered to the
.I powiat
(county) TERYT code of the point.
.TP
.B Hydrological drought
Captioned
.IR "UWAGA!" ,
e.g.
.IR "Susza hydrologiczna \(em zlewnia Rudawa" .
Filtered to the river basin containing the point, found by point\-in\-polygon
over IMGW's basin polygons (cached locally).
.PP
Relative days are shown as
.IR wczoraj ", " dzisiaj ", " jutra
instead of a date where possible; otherwise the date and time are printed.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is a flat
.I "key = value"
INI file at:
.PP
.RS 4
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pogoda\-rs/config.ini
.br
(usually
.IR ~/.config/pogoda\-rs/config.ini ).
.RE
.PP
Lines beginning with
.RB ` # "' or `" ; '
are comments;
.RI [ section ]
headers and blank lines are ignored; surrounding quotes on a value are stripped.
Recognised keys:
.TP
.B weather_place
Default location used when
.B pogoda
is run with no argument. Either a
.I City,CC
name or
.I lat,lon
coordinates, e.g.
.I "Warszawa,PL"
or
.IR "52.2298,21.0118" .
If it is unset and no argument is given,
.B pogoda
prints an error and exits non\-zero.
.TP
.B forecast_horizon
How far ahead the forecast reaches. One of:
.RS
.TP
.B tomorrow
(default) cap the window at the end of tomorrow in Polish local time. Also the
behaviour when the key is absent or holds any value other than
.IR full .
.TP
.B full
show everything IMGW provides (roughly 64 hours).
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/pogoda\-rs/config.ini
Configuration file (see
.BR CONFIGURATION ).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/pogoda\-rs/
Cached API token and IMGW river\-basin polygons. Safe to delete; it is rebuilt
on demand. Honours
.IR $XDG_CACHE_HOME .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set (to any value), colour output is disabled. Colour is also disabled
automatically when standard output is not a terminal.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Base directory for configuration. Defaults to
.I ~/.config
when unset or empty.
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Base directory for cached data. Defaults to
.I ~/.cache
when unset or empty.
.PP
.B pogoda
needs network access to reach IMGW and the geocoding services.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (a forecast was printed), or
.B \-\-help
was requested.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: an unknown option, no location given and none configured, a place that
could not be geocoded, or a network/data error talking to IMGW.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B pogoda
Forecast for the configured
.I weather_place.
.TP
.B pogoda Kraków
Forecast for a named place.
.TP
.B pogoda \(dqWarszawa,PL\(dq
Forecast for a named place, disambiguated by country code.
.TP
.B pogoda \(dq50.06,19.94\(dq
Forecast for explicit coordinates.
.SH DATA SOURCES
Forecast and warnings:
.B IMGW\-PIB
.RI ( "Instytut Meteorologii i Gospodarki Wodnej \(em PIB" ),
whose public data this tool re\-presents. Place\-name geocoding and timezone
lookup use
.BR Open\-Meteo ;
the reverse\-geocoded display name for coordinates uses
.BR BigDataCloud .
.SH SEE ALSO
Project README and
.IR config.example.ini .
Data portals:
.I https://meteo.imgw.pl
and
.IR https://danepubliczne.imgw.pl .
